!!! ===================================================================
!!! 15-telemetry-relay.matrix
!!!
!!! A complete single-file Matrix application, written to exercise every
!!! proposed construct at once. It is the stress test for the surface: if a
!!! spelling reads badly here, it reads badly everywhere.
!!!
!!! WHAT IT DOES
!!!
!!! A telemetry relay. Sensor frames arrive as a packed 32-bit header word
!!! plus a byte payload. The relay unpacks the header with bitwise
!!! manipulation, validates it, converts it to network byte order through
!!! inline assembly, stages the payload in an owned buffer, folds a CRC-32
!!! over it, encodes the samples in parallel, and dispatches the result
!!! through a class hierarchy of sinks. Malformed frames raise typed faults.
!!!
!!! HEADER LAYOUT (32 bits, packed into a "long" so bit 31 is not a sign bit)
!!!
!!!     bits 31..28   version   4 bits
!!!     bits 27..24   kind      4 bits
!!!     bits 23..8    length   16 bits
!!!     bits  7..0    flags     8 bits
!!!
!!! FEATURE INVENTORY
!!!
!!!     book, read (all four forms), library-free single file
!!!     book globals, public and private, and :: qualification
!!!     constants, immutable values, mutable variables
!!!     records, nested records, generic records, type aliases
!!!     choices with payloads, unit variants, generic choices
!!!     classes: abstract, virtual, overriding, private methods,
!!!              multiple inheritance, ancestor views, "my" receiver
!!!     contracts, implementations, inherent implementations,
!!!              generic bounds, associated functions
!!!     faults: raise, typed handlers, guards, catch-all tokens,
!!!              re-raise, "always" cleanup, cleanup that replaces an exit
!!!     owned buffers, shared and exclusive borrows, moves
!!!     raw pointers: allocate, index, release
!!!     bitwise: and, or, xor, not, shifted left by, shifted right by
!!!     arrays, array literals, indexing, length, push
!!!     every control-flow form, statement and expression
!!!     named arguments, variadic tails, mutable parameters, recursion
!!!     paragraph values and anonymous paragraphs
!!!     parallel apply across, clock operations
!!!     inline assembly, intrinsics, annotations, agent context, tests
!!!
!!! ROUTE HONESTY
!!!
!!! Three things here are deliberately route-limited, inherited from Ny and
!!! not introduced by Matrix. They are marked again at their use sites.
!!!   1. Inline assembly is x86_64 native only. Interpreted routes reject it.
!!!   2. Scalar-to-text conversion is interpreted-route only.
!!!   3. Paragraph values and anonymous paragraphs are interpreted-route only.
!!! A native build of this file would need those three sites replaced.
!!! ===================================================================

book relay.telemetry

!!! --- Links -------------------------------------------------------------
!!! All four forms appear here. The path is an book name, never a file path.

read ny.lang.core
read ny.lang.io
read ny.lang.math as math
read everything from ny.lang.collections


!!! --- Book constants and globals ---------------------------------------
!!!
!!! Book-level initialisers run in declaration order, not lexical name order.
!!! An initialiser may read an earlier one in the same book. A typed forward
!!! reference type-checks and still fails at runtime if it reads before
!!! initialisation; Matrix does not invent a zero.

constant EXPECTED-VERSION   as override long is 2
constant VERSION-SHIFT    as override long is 28
constant KIND-SHIFT       as override long is 24
constant LENGTH-SHIFT     as override long is 8
constant NIBBLE-MASK      as override long is 0x0F
constant BYTE-MASK        as override long is 0xFF
constant SHORT-MASK       as override long is 0xFFFF
constant WORD-MASK        as override long is 0xFFFFFFFF

!!! The reflected CRC-32 polynomial will not fit in an integer, so it is a
!!! long. Matrix has no u32, because Ny rejects u32 arithmetic.
constant CRC-POLYNOMIAL   as override long is 0xEDB88320
constant CRC-SEED         as override long is 0xFFFFFFFF

constant MAX-PAYLOAD      as override integer is 64
constant FLAG-URGENT      as override long is 0x01
constant FLAG-RETRANSMIT  as override long is 0x02
constant FLAG-ENCRYPTED   as override long is 0x04

!!! A public global has "relay.telemetry::name" storage identity in NIL.
!!! Another book may declare "frames-seen" without sharing this storage.
public variable frames-seen     as override integer is 0
public variable frames-rejected as override integer is 0

!!! Private to this book: no "public" modifier.
variable relay-epoch as override long is 0

!!! Aggregate globals remain interpreter-only, so the relay keeps its
!!! aggregate state in locals and passes it explicitly.


!!! --- Type aliases ------------------------------------------------------

microvolts means override long
sensor-id   means override integer


!!! --- Records -----------------------------------------------------------
!!!
!!! Every construction initialises every declared field exactly once. There
!!! is no field-default spelling, because Ny rejects field defaults.

frame-header begin record
    field version as override long
    field kind    as override long
    field length  as override long
    field flags   as override long
end record

!!! A nested record field holds a nominally typed object handle. Updating it
!!! through a field or a reference is visible through its other aliases: this
!!! is shared handle behaviour, not by-value copying.
frame begin record
    field header  as frame-header
    field sensor  as sensor-id
    field samples as array of override long
end record

measurement begin record
    field sensor   as sensor-id
    field reading  as microvolts
    field checksum as override long
end record

dispatch-stats begin record
    field accepted as override integer
    field rejected as override integer
    field checksum as override long
end record

!!! A generic record. Only concrete instantiations with supported field
!!! layouts are executed.
envelope of type T begin record
    field item     as T
    field recorded as override long
end record


!!! --- Choices -----------------------------------------------------------
!!!
!!! A variant is introduced by "when", the same word that selects one later.
!!! Declaring a case and matching a case are the same relation -- "in the case
!!! of" -- so they share the word.
!!!
!!! The payload type is introduced by "holding", not "give", so that the
!!! declaration and the pattern that destructures it read as mirror images:
!!!
!!!     when Sample holding long                    !!! declares the payload
!!!     when frame-kind.Sample holding v then ...   !!! binds the payload
!!!
!!! "give" is reserved for a value leaving the construct the reader is inside.
!!! A payload type is not a value and does not leave anything.

frame-kind begin choice
    when Heartbeat
    when Sample    holding override long
    when Batch     holding override integer
    when Shutdown  holding override integer
end choice

severity begin choice
    when Info
    when Warning holding override integer
    when Critical holding override integer
end choice

!!! A generic choice. The standard library already supplies Option and
!!! Result; redeclaring them in an application is a mistake in Matrix for the
!!! same reason it is in Ny. This one carries a distinct payload shape.
decoded of type T begin choice
    when Accepted holding T
    when Dropped  holding override integer
end choice


!!! --- Fault payloads ----------------------------------------------------
!!!
!!! A payload is a fully initialised concrete record. Scalars, class
!!! instances, choice values and raw pointers are not payloads. A handler
!!! matches exact canonical record identity, including book and concrete
!!! generic arguments.

malformed-frame begin record
    field reason as text
    field word   as override long
end record

checksum-mismatch begin record
    field expected as override long
    field actual   as override long
end record

sink-unavailable begin record
    field sink as text
end record


!!! --- Contracts ---------------------------------------------------------
!!!
!!! Implementations use static dispatch. There are no dynamic contract
!!! objects, because NIL does not execute them. Default method bodies,
!!! supertraits and associated types have no spelling.

describable begin contract
    describe returns text
end contract

scoring begin contract
    score returns override long
    rescore receives weight as override long on mutable receiver returns nothing
end contract

sizable begin contract
    byte-width without receiver returns override integer
end contract


!!! =====================================================================
!!! SECTION 1 -- Bit manipulation
!!!
!!! Word operators are deliberately wordy. This section is the honest cost
!!! of that choice: judge the surface here more than anywhere else.
!!! =====================================================================

context "Packs a telemetry header into one 32-bit word."
context "version and kind are 4 bits each, length is 16 bits, flags are 8."
context "Callers must mask their own inputs; this function truncates."
note inline
pack-header receives version as override long, kind as override long, length as override long, flags as override long returns override long begin paragraph
    value v is (version bitwise and NIBBLE-MASK) shifted left by VERSION-SHIFT
    value k is (kind    bitwise and NIBBLE-MASK) shifted left by KIND-SHIFT
    value l is (length  bitwise and SHORT-MASK)  shifted left by LENGTH-SHIFT
    value f is  flags   bitwise and BYTE-MASK
    give ((v bitwise or k) bitwise or l) bitwise or f
end paragraph

context "Extracts the 4-bit version field from a packed header word."
header-version receives word as override long returns override long begin paragraph
    give (word shifted right by VERSION-SHIFT) bitwise and NIBBLE-MASK
end paragraph

header-kind receives word as override long returns override long begin paragraph
    give (word shifted right by KIND-SHIFT) bitwise and NIBBLE-MASK
end paragraph

header-length receives word as override long returns override long begin paragraph
    give (word shifted right by LENGTH-SHIFT) bitwise and SHORT-MASK
end paragraph

header-flags receives word as override long returns override long begin paragraph
    give word bitwise and BYTE-MASK
end paragraph

!!! "bitwise not" is the unary complement. Masking afterwards keeps the
!!! result inside the 32-bit window, because "long" is 64 bits wide.
invert-flags receives word as override long returns override long begin paragraph
    give (bitwise not word) bitwise and WORD-MASK
end paragraph

has-flag receives word as override long, flag as override long returns boolean begin paragraph
    give (header-flags with word being word) bitwise and flag does not equal 0
end paragraph

!!! A population count by shifting. This is the kind of loop Matrix exists
!!! to make unambiguous: no precedence, no operator overloading, no
!!! off-by-one hidden in a compound assignment.
count-set-bits receives word as override long returns override integer begin paragraph
    variable remaining as override long is word bitwise and WORD-MASK
    variable total     as override integer is 0
    repeat while remaining does not equal 0
        when remaining bitwise and 1 equals 1 then
            set total to total plus 1
        end when
        set remaining to remaining shifted right by 1
    end repeat
    give total
end paragraph


!!! =====================================================================
!!! SECTION 2 -- Inline assembly
!!!
!!! x86_64 native only. Register-only, "long" operands, at most eight inputs
!!! and one output, drawn from the approved AT&T integer instruction list.
!!! Interpreted routes, interpreter libraries and the NIL debugger reject this
!!! operation with a native-route diagnostic; they never emulate it.
!!!
!!! bswapl is not on the approved list, so the 32-bit swap is a full 64-bit
!!! bswapq followed by a shift. With an output, $0 is the output register and
!!! $1 is the first input.
!!! =====================================================================

context "Converts a 32-bit header word to network byte order."
context "x86_64 native routes only; interpreted routes reject the assembly."
to-network-order receives word as override long returns override long begin paragraph
    variable swapped as override long is 0
    assembly for x86_64 is "movq $1, $0; bswapq $0" using (word bitwise and WORD-MASK) giving swapped
    give (swapped shifted right by 32) bitwise and WORD-MASK
end paragraph

!!! A portable equivalent, assembled from the bit operations above. The relay
!!! uses this one so the program runs on every route.
to-network-order-portable receives word as override long returns override long begin paragraph
    value masked is word bitwise and WORD-MASK
    value b0 is (masked bitwise and BYTE-MASK) shifted left by 24
    value b1 is ((masked shifted right by 8)  bitwise and BYTE-MASK) shifted left by 16
    value b2 is ((masked shifted right by 16) bitwise and BYTE-MASK) shifted left by 8
    value b3 is  (masked shifted right by 24) bitwise and BYTE-MASK
    give ((b0 bitwise or b1) bitwise or b2) bitwise or b3
end paragraph


!!! =====================================================================
!!! SECTION 3 -- Owned buffers and raw pointers
!!!
!!! Owners and views cannot be parameters, results, globals, record fields,
!!! array elements or captures, so every ownership operation in this
!!! application lives inside one function and reads scalars out to pass them
!!! elsewhere. That restriction is Ny's; Matrix expresses it in the grammar
!!! by making ownership operations statements rather than expressions.
!!! =====================================================================

context "Folds a reflected CRC-32 step over one byte. Not cryptographic."
crc-step receives accumulator as override long, sample as override long returns override long begin paragraph
    variable crc as override long is accumulator bitwise xor (sample bitwise and BYTE-MASK)
    repeat for bit from 0 to 8
        when crc bitwise and 1 equals 1 then
            set crc to (crc shifted right by 1) bitwise xor CRC-POLYNOMIAL
        otherwise
            set crc to crc shifted right by 1
        end when
    end repeat
    give crc bitwise and WORD-MASK
end paragraph

context "Stages a payload in an owned byte buffer and returns its CRC-32."
context "The buffer is freed exactly once when its final owner's scope ends."
stage-and-checksum receives samples as array of override long returns override long begin paragraph

    !!! An owned buffer is zero-initialised. A count below one requests one
    !!! element; an oversized allocation fails. Mutating it requires a
    !!! mutable owner.
    own variable staging as array of override byte sized MAX-PAYLOAD

    value count as override integer is the length of samples

    !!! One exclusive view. While it exists, no other read, write, move or
    !!! borrow of the owner is permitted. Mutability belongs to the view
    !!! type, so the view binding itself is not declared mutable. Lifetimes
    !!! are lexical, not last-use inferred: the borrow ends with the block.
    when count is greater than 0 then
        borrow writable from staging exclusively
        repeat for index from 0 to count
            when index is at least MAX-PAYLOAD then
                stop repeating
            end when
            set writable at index to ((samples at index) bitwise and BYTE-MASK) becomes override byte
        end repeat
    end when

    !!! Shared views. Several may coexist and the owner may still be read,
    !!! but writes and moves are forbidden until every view's scope ends.
    variable crc as override long is CRC-SEED
    when true then
        borrow first  from staging
        borrow second from staging
        repeat for index from 0 to count
            when index is at least MAX-PAYLOAD then
                stop repeating
            end when
            set crc to crc-step with accumulator being crc, sample being (first at index) becomes override long
        end repeat
        !!! The owner is still readable while shared views exist.
        say second at 0
        say staging at 0
    end when

    !!! A move transfers the allocation into a new binding and invalidates
    !!! the source. A move does not free storage. Control-flow checking is
    !!! conservative: if either branch of a conditional moves an owner,
    !!! later use of it is rejected.
    move staging into sealed
    say sealed at 0

    give (bitwise not crc) bitwise and WORD-MASK
end paragraph

context "Writes a header word into a raw byte buffer, big-endian."
context "Raw pointers are explicitly released; there is no borrow checking."
serialise-header receives word as override long returns override long begin paragraph

    !!! Raw pointers are the unmanaged alternative to owned buffers:
    !!! explicit allocation, explicit release, no lexical lifetime.
    allocate octets as pointer to override byte sized 4

    value ordered is to-network-order-portable with word being word
    set octets at 0 to ((ordered shifted right by 24) bitwise and BYTE-MASK) becomes override byte
    set octets at 1 to ((ordered shifted right by 16) bitwise and BYTE-MASK) becomes override byte
    set octets at 2 to ((ordered shifted right by 8)  bitwise and BYTE-MASK) becomes override byte
    set octets at 3 to  (ordered                      bitwise and BYTE-MASK) becomes override byte

    !!! Byte storage retains the low eight bits, so -1 becomes 255, 256
    !!! becomes 0 and 511 becomes 255. This is Ny's wrapping byte rule, not a
    !!! range assertion.
    variable rebuilt as override long is 0
    repeat for index from 0 to 4
        set rebuilt to (rebuilt shifted left by 8) bitwise or ((octets at index) becomes override long)
    end repeat

    release octets
    give rebuilt
end paragraph


!!! =====================================================================
!!! SECTION 4 -- Classes
!!!
!!! "my" is the receiver. Matrix synthesises the explicit first self
!!! parameter that Ny requires, so the NIL CALL_METHOD arity is identical.
!!! Generic classes, trait objects and downcasts have no spelling.
!!! =====================================================================

!!! An abstract class may be a parameter, result, field or local type, but it
!!! cannot be constructed.
abstract sink begin class
    field name     as text
    field delivered as override integer

    !!! An abstract method has no body and therefore no begin/end pair. A
    !!! class with its own abstract method must itself be declared abstract.
    public abstract accept receives reading as microvolts returns boolean

    !!! A concrete helper on an abstract class may call an abstract method on
    !!! the receiver. It keeps its declaring owner's scope, but its virtual
    !!! call selects the dynamic override.
    public relay receives reading as microvolts returns override integer begin paragraph
        when my accept with reading being reading then
            set my delivered to my delivered plus 1
        end when
        give my delivered
    end paragraph

    public label returns text begin paragraph
        give my name
    end paragraph
end class

console-sink inherits sink begin class
    field threshold as microvolts

    public replaces accept receives reading as microvolts returns boolean begin paragraph
        when reading is less than my threshold then
            give false
        end when
        say reading
        give true
    end paragraph

    !!! No modifier means private to the declaring class.
    margin returns microvolts begin paragraph
        give my threshold shifted right by 1
    end paragraph

    public headroom receives reading as microvolts returns microvolts begin paragraph
        give reading minus (my margin with nothing)
    end paragraph
end class

!!! A deeper override. An override remains virtual even where the marker is
!!! omitted; Matrix requires the marker anyway, so the intent is explicit.
counting-sink inherits console-sink begin class
    field dropped as override integer

    public replaces accept receives reading as microvolts returns boolean begin paragraph
        when reading is at most 0 then
            set my dropped to my dropped plus 1
            give false
        end when
        give true
    end paragraph
end class

!!! Multiple inheritance uses the actual concrete field layout, not an assumed
!!! first-base prefix. Cycles, ambiguous fields, ambiguous inherited methods,
!!! incompatible overrides, reduced visibility and hiding a nonvirtual
!!! inherited method are all rejected.
tagged begin class
    field tag as text

    public tag-of returns text begin paragraph
        give my tag
    end paragraph
end class

tagged-sink inherits counting-sink, tagged begin class
    public replaces accept receives reading as microvolts returns boolean begin paragraph
        give reading is greater than 0
    end paragraph

    public identity returns text begin paragraph
        give my tag-of with nothing
    end paragraph
end class


!!! =====================================================================
!!! SECTION 5 -- Implementations
!!! =====================================================================

measurement provides describable begin implementation
    describe returns text begin paragraph
        give "measurement"
    end paragraph
end implementation

measurement provides scoring begin implementation
    score returns override long begin paragraph
        give my reading bitwise xor my checksum
    end paragraph

    rescore receives weight as override long on mutable receiver returns nothing begin paragraph
        set my reading to my reading times weight
    end paragraph
end implementation

measurement provides sizable begin implementation
    byte-width without receiver returns override integer begin paragraph
        give 20
    end paragraph
end implementation

!!! An inherent implementation block, with no contract named. Extra concrete
!!! helpers are allowed and do not become contract requirements.
measurement begin implementation
    urgent returns boolean begin paragraph
        give my checksum bitwise and FLAG-URGENT does not equal 0
    end paragraph
end implementation

frame-header begin implementation
    packed returns override long begin paragraph
        give pack-header with version being my version, kind being my kind, length being my length, flags being my flags
    end paragraph
end implementation

!!! A generic implementation constrained by a bound. The bound restricts which
!!! concrete types may instantiate the generic code; it does not relax the
!!! native layout restrictions, which still apply independently.
envelope of type T meeting scoring begin implementation
    weighted-score returns override long begin paragraph
        give (my item.score with nothing) plus my recorded
    end paragraph
end implementation

envelope of type T meeting describable begin implementation
    caption returns text begin paragraph
        give my item.describe with nothing
    end paragraph
end implementation

!!! An associated function has no receiver and may be called through a
!!! bounded type parameter. Two different bounds exposing the same associated
!!! function are ambiguous and are rejected rather than resolved by
!!! declaration order.
default-width of type T meeting sizable returns override integer begin paragraph
    give T.byte-width with nothing
end paragraph


!!! =====================================================================
!!! SECTION 6 -- Parallel workers
!!!
!!! A worker and its entire transitive call graph may use scalar arithmetic,
!!! bitwise operations, comparisons, scalar casts, locals, branches, loops
!!! and direct calls to other isolated scalar helpers. They may NOT touch
!!! globals, pointers, owned buffers, views, record handles, arrays, text,
!!! class methods, a nested apply, assembly, foreign calls, console or file
!!! I/O, process operations, clocks, sleeps or fault payloads.
!!!
!!! None of the functions below reads an book global. That is not a style
!!! choice: the restriction is checked on NIL as well as source, so
!!! hand-written NIL cannot grant a worker additional effects.
!!! =====================================================================

!!! The mask literals below are written out rather than read from the book
!!! constants above, and that is NOT a style choice. A book constant is a
!!! global, so reading one emits LOAD_GLOBAL, which the parallel contract
!!! forbids inside a worker's transitive call graph. Ny checks this on the NIL
!!! artifact as well as on source, so neither --no-typecheck nor hand-written
!!! NIL can grant a worker the extra effect.
!!!
!!! This file originally did read SHORT-MASK and WORD-MASK here, and the
!!! verifier rejected it with:
!!!
!!!     worker 'relay__telemetry__encode_sample' contains non-isolated
!!!     operation 'LOAD_GLOBAL'
clamp-sample receives sample as override long returns override long begin paragraph
    when sample is less than 0 then
        give 0
    end when
    when sample is greater than 0xFFFF then
        give 0xFFFF
    end when
    give sample
end paragraph

whiten-sample receives sample as override long returns override long begin paragraph
    value clamped is clamp-sample with sample being sample
    give (clamped bitwise xor (clamped shifted right by 7)) bitwise and 0xFFFF
end paragraph

context "Isolated scalar worker: scales, whitens and masks one sample."
encode-sample receives raw as override long returns override long begin paragraph
    give (whiten-sample with sample being (raw times 3)) bitwise and 0xFFFFFFFF
end paragraph


!!! =====================================================================
!!! SECTION 7 -- Faults
!!!
!!! "always" is Ny's "recover": cleanup with finally semantics, not an
!!! additional handler. It runs once on normal exit, after a selected
!!! handler, on unmatched propagation, and through give, stop repeating or
!!! continue repeating.
!!! =====================================================================

context "Validates a packed header word and returns its unpacked record."
context "Raises malformed-frame for a bad version, kind or declared length."
validate-header receives word as override long returns frame-header begin paragraph
    value version is header-version with word being word
    value kind    is header-kind    with word being word
    value length  is header-length  with word being word
    value flags   is header-flags   with word being word

    when version does not equal EXPECTED-VERSION then
        raise malformed-frame with reason being "unsupported version", word being word
    end when

    when kind is greater than 3 then
        raise malformed-frame with reason being "unknown kind", word being word
    end when

    when length is greater than (MAX-PAYLOAD becomes override long) then
        raise malformed-frame with reason being "payload too long", word being word
    end when

    give build frame-header with version being version, kind being kind, length being length, flags being flags
end paragraph

context "Verifies a payload checksum, raising checksum-mismatch on failure."
verify-checksum receives expected as override long, actual as override long returns nothing begin paragraph
    when expected does not equal actual then
        raise checksum-mismatch with expected being expected, actual being actual
    end when
end paragraph

!!! Handlers are tried in source order. A guard must be boolean; a false
!!! guard proceeds to the next handler. The binding is visible in its own
!!! guard and body only -- not in sibling handlers and not in "always".
!!! Cleanup resources are declared outside the attempt, because attempt-body
!!! bindings are not visible to handlers or to cleanup.
context "Decodes one frame, converting every fault into a decoded result."
decode-frame receives word as override long, samples as array of override long returns decoded of override long begin paragraph
    variable attempts as override integer is 0

    attempt
        set attempts to attempts plus 1
        value header is validate-header with word being word
        value folded is stage-and-checksum with samples being samples
        evaluate verify-checksum with expected being folded, actual being folded
        set relay.telemetry::frames-seen to relay.telemetry::frames-seen plus 1
        give decoded.Accepted holding folded

    caught malformed-frame as problem provided problem.reason does not equal ""
        say problem.reason
        set relay.telemetry::frames-rejected to relay.telemetry::frames-rejected plus 1
        give decoded.Dropped holding 1

    caught malformed-frame as problem
        say "malformed frame"
        give decoded.Dropped holding 2

    caught checksum-mismatch as problem
        say problem.expected
        say problem.actual
        give decoded.Dropped holding 3

    always
        say attempts
    end attempt
end paragraph

!!! A catch-all binds an opaque token. The token may be ignored, or it may be
!!! the complete expression of a re-raise. Reading its fields, printing it,
!!! copying it, casting it, giving it or passing it onward is rejected. An
!!! unguarded catch-all must be the final handler. A retained token can be
!!! re-raised more than once if an inner attempt handles each re-raise.
context "Re-raises any fault after logging that the relay saw one."
relay-or-reraise receives word as override long, samples as array of override long returns decoded of override long begin paragraph
    attempt
        give decode-frame with word being word, samples being samples
    caught anything as token
        say "relay observed a fault"
        raise token again
    end attempt
end paragraph

!!! A give or raise inside "always" replaces the suspended exit. This can
!!! deliberately suppress an earlier fault or result -- shown here on purpose,
!!! because it is the single most surprising rule in the fault contract.
context "Demonstrates cleanup replacing a suspended fault. Never raises."
suppressing-exit returns override integer begin paragraph
    attempt
        raise sink-unavailable with sink being "console"
    always
        give minus 1
    end attempt
end paragraph


!!! =====================================================================
!!! SECTION 8 -- Variadics, recursion, mutable parameters
!!! =====================================================================

context "Folds a CRC over a variadic list of samples."
checksum-of receives more samples as override long returns override long begin paragraph
    variable crc   as override long is CRC-SEED
    variable index as override integer is 0
    repeat while index is less than (the length of samples)
        set crc to crc-step with accumulator being crc, sample being (samples at index)
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give (bitwise not crc) bitwise and WORD-MASK
end paragraph

!!! A mutable parameter is the callee's own binding. It does not mutate the
!!! caller's scalar.
normalise-in-place receives variable sample as override long, floor as override long returns override long begin paragraph
    when sample is less than floor then
        set sample to floor
    end when
    give sample
end paragraph

!!! Ordinary recursion. The parameter default is retained in the syntax tree
!!! and restricted to a literal atom; Ny currently rejects omitted arguments
!!! at the call site, so every caller still passes every parameter.
fold-depth receives depth as override integer defaulting to 1 returns override integer begin paragraph
    when depth is at most 1 then
        give 1
    end when
    give depth times (fold-depth with depth being depth minus 1)
end paragraph


!!! =====================================================================
!!! SECTION 9 -- Intrinsics
!!!
!!! A runtime-backed declaration has no body. The annotation is not an
!!! implementation: the named provider must exist on every claimed route.
!!! =====================================================================

note intrinsic "console.writeln"
write-line receives line as text


!!! =====================================================================
!!! SECTION 10 -- Dispatch
!!! =====================================================================

context "Dispatches one reading through an ancestor-typed sink."
context "The static view controls available members; the dynamic class"
context "controls which override actually runs."
dispatch receives target as sink, reading as microvolts returns override integer begin paragraph
    give target.relay with reading being reading
end paragraph

context "Summarises a batch of readings against one sink."
summarise receives target as sink, readings as array of override long returns dispatch-stats begin paragraph
    variable accepted as override integer is 0
    variable rejected as override integer is 0
    variable folded   as override long is CRC-SEED

    repeat for each reading in readings
        value before is target.relay with reading being reading
        when before is greater than accepted then
            set accepted to before
        otherwise
            set rejected to rejected plus 1
        end when
        set folded to crc-step with accumulator being folded, sample being reading
    end repeat

    give build dispatch-stats with accepted being accepted, rejected being rejected, checksum being ((bitwise not folded) bitwise and WORD-MASK)
end paragraph


!!! =====================================================================
!!! SECTION 11 -- Entry point
!!! =====================================================================

main returns number begin paragraph

    say "MATRIX TELEMETRY RELAY"

    !!! --- Clock ---------------------------------------------------------
    !!! A nonpositive duration is an immediate no-op. Real and text
    !!! durations are rejected rather than silently converted.
    value started as override long is now in milliseconds
    set relay-epoch to started

    !!! --- Bit packing ---------------------------------------------------
    value flags as override long is (FLAG-URGENT bitwise or FLAG-ENCRYPTED)
    value word  as override long is pack-header with version being EXPECTED-VERSION, kind being 1, length being 8, flags being flags

    say header-version with word being word
    say header-kind    with word being word
    say header-length  with word being word
    say header-flags   with word being word
    say has-flag with word being word, flag being FLAG-URGENT
    say has-flag with word being word, flag being FLAG-RETRANSMIT
    say count-set-bits with word being word
    say invert-flags with word being word

    !!! --- Byte order and raw pointers ------------------------------------
    say to-network-order-portable with word being word
    say serialise-header with word being word

    !!! --- Records and nested records -------------------------------------
    value header is build frame-header with version being EXPECTED-VERSION, kind being 1, length being 8, flags being flags
    say header.packed with nothing

    value samples as array of override long is [
        17 becomes override long,
        42 becomes override long,
        255 becomes override long,
        1024 becomes override long
    ]

    variable frame is build frame with header being header, sensor being 7, samples being samples
    say frame.header.version
    say frame.sensor
    say frame.samples at 2
    say the length of frame.samples

    !!! Record handles are shared, so a mutation through the nested field is
    !!! visible through the original binding.
    set frame.header.flags to FLAG-RETRANSMIT
    say header.flags

    !!! --- Arrays ----------------------------------------------------------
    variable readings as array of override long is []
    append (120 becomes override long) to readings
    append (minus 5 becomes override long) to readings
    append (900 becomes override long) to readings
    say the length of readings

    !!! An out-of-range read yields the element's zero value and an
    !!! out-of-range write is a no-op. This is Ny's behaviour, inherited.
    say readings at 99

    !!! --- Owned buffers and checksums -------------------------------------
    value folded is stage-and-checksum with samples being samples
    say folded
    say checksum-of with more 17 becomes override long, 42 becomes override long
    say checksum-of with nothing

    !!! --- Parallel apply ---------------------------------------------------
    !!! Results occupy the same indices as their inputs, the input array is
    !!! not mutated, and the caller receives the result array only after
    !!! every worker thread has finished. There are no task handles.
    value encoded is apply encode-sample across samples
    repeat for index from 0 to (the length of encoded)
        say encoded at index
    end repeat

    !!! An empty input returns an empty array without starting a worker.
    value idle as array of override long is []
    value no-work is apply encode-sample across idle
    say the length of no-work

    !!! --- Classes and ancestor views ----------------------------------------
    !!! An ancestor view changes the static view, not the dynamic class or the
    !!! field storage. There is no slicing and no implicit copy. A
    !!! Sink-typed parameter never becomes a derived type merely because a
    !!! derived object was passed.
    variable console is build console-sink with name being "console", delivered being 0, threshold being (100 becomes override long)
    variable counting is build counting-sink with name being "counting", delivered being 0, threshold being (50 becomes override long), dropped being 0
    variable tagged is build tagged-sink with name being "tagged", delivered being 0, threshold being (10 becomes override long), dropped being 0, tag being "edge"

    value as-sink as sink is console
    say dispatch with target being as-sink, reading being (240 becomes override long)
    say dispatch with target being as-sink, reading being (10 becomes override long)
    say as-sink.label with nothing
    say console.headroom with reading being (240 becomes override long)

    value counting-view as sink is counting
    say dispatch with target being counting-view, reading being (minus 3 becomes override long)
    say counting.dropped

    value tagged-view as sink is tagged
    say dispatch with target being tagged-view, reading being (5 becomes override long)
    say tagged.identity with nothing

    !!! AN ARRAY OF CLASS HANDLES IS NOT EXECUTABLE on the interpreted route,
    !!! so there is no loop over sinks here. Written as
    !!!
    !!!     value sinks as array of sink is [as-sink, counting-view, tagged-view]
    !!!
    !!! it compiles to 'NEW_ARRAY_LITERAL 3 sink' and the VM rejects it with
    !!! "class value cannot be used by this untyped, scalar, or raw-pointer
    !!! operation". A hand-written Ny equivalent fails identically, so this is
    !!! a NIL route limitation rather than anything Matrix introduces -- worth
    !!! knowing, because classes.md says aliases "remain aliases through
    !!! collection", which overstates what the interpreter executes.
    !!!
    !!! Dispatch through each ancestor-typed value directly instead.
    say as-sink.label with nothing
    say counting-view.label with nothing
    say tagged-view.label with nothing

    value stats is summarise with target being counting-view, readings being readings
    say stats.accepted
    say stats.rejected
    say stats.checksum

    !!! --- Contracts and generics --------------------------------------------
    variable reading is build measurement with sensor being 7, reading being (480 becomes override long), checksum being folded
    say reading.describe with nothing
    say reading.score with nothing
    say reading.urgent with nothing
    evaluate reading.rescore with weight being (2 becomes override long)
    say reading.reading
    say measurement.byte-width with nothing
    say default-width of measurement with nothing

    value boxed is build envelope of measurement with item being reading, recorded being started
    say boxed.caption with nothing
    say boxed.weighted-score with nothing

    !!! --- Choices ------------------------------------------------------------
    value kind as frame-kind is frame-kind.Sample holding (42 becomes override long)
    consider kind
        when frame-kind.Heartbeat then say "heartbeat"
        when frame-kind.Sample holding sample-value provided sample-value is greater than 40 then say "large sample"
        when frame-kind.Sample holding sample-value then say "sample"
        when frame-kind.Batch holding count then say count
        when frame-kind.Shutdown holding code then say code
        otherwise say "unknown kind"
    end consider

    value level as severity is severity.Warning holding 3
    value level-name as text is consider level
        when severity.Info give "info"
        when severity.Warning holding code give "warning"
        when severity.Critical holding code give "critical"
        otherwise give "unclassified"
    end consider
    say level-name

    !!! --- Faults --------------------------------------------------------------
    value good is decode-frame with word being word, samples being samples
    consider good
        when decoded.Accepted holding checksum then say checksum
        when decoded.Dropped holding code then say code
    end consider

    !!! A bad version word: version 9 instead of 2.
    value bad-word is pack-header with version being 9, kind being 1, length being 8, flags being 0
    value bad is decode-frame with word being bad-word, samples being samples
    consider bad
        when decoded.Accepted holding checksum then say checksum
        when decoded.Dropped holding code then say code
    end consider

    !!! A re-raise caught at the call site. An exact nominal match includes
    !!! book and concrete generic arguments: equally named records in
    !!! different books do not match each other.
    attempt
        value relayed is relay-or-reraise with word being bad-word, samples being samples
        consider relayed
            when decoded.Accepted holding checksum then say checksum
            when decoded.Dropped holding code then say code
        end consider
    caught malformed-frame as problem
        say problem.reason
    caught anything as token
        say "unexpected fault class"
    end attempt

    say suppressing-exit with nothing

    !!! --- Control flow, every form ---------------------------------------------
    variable countdown as override integer is 3
    repeat while countdown is greater than 0
        say countdown
        set countdown to countdown minus 1
    end repeat

    repeat for step from 0 to 5
        when step equals 2 then
            continue repeating
        end when
        when step equals 4 then
            stop repeating
        end when
        say step
    end repeat

    value labels as array of text is ["alpha", "beta", "gamma"]
    repeat for each label in labels
        say label
    end repeat

    variable budget as override integer is 2
    repeat forever
        when budget is at most 0 then
            stop repeating
        end when
        set budget to budget minus 1
    end repeat

    !!! Conditional expression, and the statement form with every branch.
    value verdict as text is when stats.accepted is greater than 0 give "delivering" otherwise give "idle" end when
    say verdict

    when relay.telemetry::frames-seen is greater than 0 then
        say "frames accepted"
    otherwise when relay.telemetry::frames-rejected is greater than 0 then
        say "all frames rejected"
    otherwise
        say "no frames"
    end when

    !!! --- Mutable parameters, recursion, paragraph values -------------------------
    value floor-value as override long is 100
    value raised is normalise-in-place with sample being (7 becomes override long), floor being floor-value
    say raised
    say fold-depth with depth being 5

    !!! The paragraph-value demonstration lives in its own paragraph,
    !!! declared after main. It CANNOT sit here, because main contains
    !!! attempt blocks and an indirect call is rejected inside any
    !!! fault-bearing function:
    !!!
    !!!     call in a fault-bearing function lacks a supported exact
    !!!     result signature
    !!!
    !!! Hand-written Ny fails the same way, so this is an undocumented
    !!! interaction between two NIL features rather than anything Matrix
    !!! introduces. Keep indirect calls out of fault-handling paragraphs.
    say paragraph-values with nothing

    !!! --- Intrinsic and clock ------------------------------------------------------
    evaluate write-line with line being "relay drained"
    sleep for 5 milliseconds
    value finished as override long is now in milliseconds
    say finished is at least started

    say relay.telemetry::frames-seen
    say relay.telemetry::frames-rejected
    give 0
end paragraph


context "Paragraph values and anonymous paragraphs, kept clear of faults."
context "Interpreted routes only: native indirect calls are not implemented."
paragraph-values returns override long begin paragraph
    value folder is the paragraph crc-step
    value folded is folder with accumulator being CRC-SEED, sample being (42 becomes override long)

    value doubler is anonymous receives n as override long returns override long begin paragraph
        give n shifted left by 1
    end paragraph
    value doubled is doubler with n being (21 becomes override long)

    give folded bitwise xor doubled
end paragraph


!!! =====================================================================
!!! SECTION 12 -- Tests
!!!
!!! A test block lowers to Ny's test declaration and sets function flag
!!! bit 1. These are registered in the NIL module's test registry.
!!! =====================================================================

header-round-trips begin test
    value word is pack-header with version being 2, kind being 3, length being 64, flags being 5
    say header-version with word being word
    say header-kind    with word being word
    say header-length  with word being word
    say header-flags   with word being word
end test

byte-order-is-reversible begin test
    value word is pack-header with version being 2, kind being 1, length being 8, flags being 1
    value once  is to-network-order-portable with word being word
    value twice is to-network-order-portable with word being once
    say twice equals word
end test

bit-counting-is-exact begin test
    say count-set-bits with word being 0xFF
    say count-set-bits with word being 0
    say count-set-bits with word being WORD-MASK
end test

malformed-frames-are-rejected begin test
    value bad is pack-header with version being 9, kind being 1, length being 8, flags being 0
    attempt
        evaluate validate-header with word being bad
        say "unexpectedly accepted"
    caught malformed-frame as problem
        say problem.reason
    end attempt
end test
